 ### Foreground-Background Fusion
-A module combining foreground and background features to preserve details from the dense surface points and handle large scenes via the bounded domain. It consists of several layers of multi-layer perceptrons [S3]. It concatenates the 128-dimensional foreground feature and 128-dimensional background feature, then passes them through 4 MLP layers to get the color of the rendered point [S3]. The rendering loss is supervised using an L2 loss between rendered pixels $r_p$ and ground truth $r_g$: $L_R = ||r_p - r_g||^2$ [S3]. The second stage training uses an Adam optimizer with an initial learning rate $5 \times 10^{-4}$ for $2 \times 10^6$ iterations, approximately 20 hours on a single A100 GPU [S3].
+A module combining foreground and background features to preserve details from the dense surface points and handle large scenes via the bounded domain [S3]. It consists of several layers of multi-layer perceptrons [S3]. It concatenates the 128-dimensional foreground feature and 128-dimensional background feature, then passes them through 4 MLP layers to get the color of the rendered point [S3]. The rendering loss is supervised using an L2 loss between rendered pixels $r_p$ and ground truth $r_g$: $L_R = ||r_p - r_g||^2$ [S3]. The second stage training uses an Adam optimizer with an initial learning rate $5 \times 10^{-4}$ for $2 \times 10^6$ iterations, approximately 20 hours on a single A100 GPU [S3].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the nearest neighbor search for LiDAR points and hash grid queries. Not given in the sources.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the size of the hash grid and the storage of LiDAR points. Not given in the sources.
-*   **Strengths:** Robustness in low-texture regions due to LiDAR geometric priors; efficient representation via hash encoding. Not given in the sources.
